      "Fouta Djallon's centuries-old written Fulfulde-in-Arabic-script literary and legal tradition represents one of West Africa's most sustained indigenous Islamic scholarly cultures, comparable in seriousness, if less internationally famous, to Timbuktu's manuscript tradition."
