      "Home to Balanta, Fula, Mandinka, Papel, and other peoples; the earliest documented inhabitants were the Jola, Papel, Manjak, Balanta, and Biafada, who were progressively pushed toward the coast and onto the Bijagós islands as Mandinka migrants arrived in the 13th century and Fulani in the 15th, while the coastal Bijagós archipelago itself maintained a distinct matrilineal culture and history of resisting outside political control."
