      "The ruins of Kansala, Kaabu's exploded capital, survive today east of Bafatá as a little-visited but historically resonant site, and the National Ethnographic Museum in Bissau holds collections of Bijagó masks, Balanta agricultural tools, and Mandinka textiles spanning this whole layered history."
