      "Within Niumi, the village of Jufureh was founded in the early 1500s by Samba Taal, a Muslim Torodbe cleric from Futa Toro (in modern Senegal), predating recorded Portuguese contact in the area; by the mid-18th century Jufureh had done business for generations with slave traders on nearby James Island, rather than existing in isolation from that trade."
